{
  How to describe your display (the full guide is DOCs/WiringGuide.md):

    One display per HUB75 adapter. The first adapter drives DISP0, the second DISP1, the third DISP2.

    1. Say once for the display: the adapter's pin group, the panel driver chip, one panel's
       columns and rows, and the colour depth.
    2. List the panels in cable order, one LONG sentence per panel. The first sentence is the
       panel the adapter plugs into, the next is the panel its ribbon cable goes to, and so on.
       A sentence says where the panel sits and which way its own top points, as you see it
       from the front:
           LONG    hwEnum.ROW_1 | hwEnum.COL_0 | hwEnum.TOP_DOWN
       Row 0 is the top row of panels and column 0 the left column.
    3. Not sure? Write every panel as hwEnum.ROW_0 | hwEnum.COL_k | hwEnum.TOP_UP (k = 0, 1, 2 ...),
       run demo_hub75_numberPanels, and copy what each panel shows: its place on the wall and
       which way its arrow points. Run it again: the labels then read in order and every arrow
       points up.

    Join the words with | only. A cube: mark its top face hwEnum.CUBE_TOP and its front face
    hwEnum.CUBE_FRONT. The panels must form one piece: each shares a full edge with the rest.

    Only the displays you have are described. A second or third display, and each optional
    setting, is switched on with one #DEFINE line next to it (see the templates below DISP0):
        #DEFINE DISP1_PRESENT         then the DISP1 block
        #DEFINE DISPn_ROTATED         then DISPn_ROTATION = hwEnum.TOP_TO_RIGHT (or TOP_TO_LEFT,
                                      TOP_TO_BOTTOM): the display, built and identified, is hung turned
        #DEFINE DISPn_REFRESH_GIVEN   then DISPn_TARGET_REFRESH_HZ = <Hz> (default 60)

    What the compiler says when a #DEFINE and its setting do not match:
        setting written, #DEFINE missing   - Symbol is already defined (m541), at the setting's
                                             default in the Defaults section below
        #DEFINE written, setting missing   - Expected an object constant, structure, or method
                                             (reported in isp_hub75_hwBufferAccess.spin2)
        DISP1_PRESENT, no DISP1 block      - Undefined symbol (in the storage section below)

    Everything below the USER SECTION is not edited.
}

' ==================================== USER SECTION ====================================

CON ' ---- DISP0: the display on the 1st HUB75 adapter ----
    {Spin2_Doc_CON}

    DISP0_ADAPTER_BASE_PIN  = hwEnum.PIN_GROUP_P16_P31
    DISP0_PANEL_DRIVER_CHIP = hwEnum.CHIP_ICN2037
    DISP0_PANEL_COLUMNS     = 128
    DISP0_PANEL_ROWS        = 64
    ' hub RAM per pixel: 3 screen-buffer bytes plus one byte per bit of depth (11 bytes at 8 bits);
    ' lower the depth only when the display does not fit
    DISP0_COLOR_DEPTH       = hwEnum.DEPTH_8BIT

DAT ' ---- DISP0 panels, in cable order ----

'  Seen from the front, every panel hung upside-down; the adapter plugs into the bottom-left panel:
'     [C2][C3]
'     [C0][C1]
disp0Panels     LONG    hwEnum.ROW_1 | hwEnum.COL_0 | hwEnum.TOP_DOWN
                LONG    hwEnum.ROW_1 | hwEnum.COL_1 | hwEnum.TOP_DOWN
                LONG    hwEnum.ROW_0 | hwEnum.COL_0 | hwEnum.TOP_DOWN
                LONG    hwEnum.ROW_0 | hwEnum.COL_1 | hwEnum.TOP_DOWN
disp0PanelsEnd

' ---- A second display: remove the leading ' from each line below, then edit it ----
'#DEFINE DISP1_PRESENT
'CON
'    DISP1_ADAPTER_BASE_PIN  = hwEnum.PIN_GROUP_P32_P47
'    DISP1_PANEL_DRIVER_CHIP = hwEnum.CHIP_FM6126A
'    DISP1_PANEL_COLUMNS     = 64
'    DISP1_PANEL_ROWS        = 32
'    DISP1_COLOR_DEPTH       = hwEnum.DEPTH_8BIT
'DAT
'disp1Panels     LONG    hwEnum.ROW_0 | hwEnum.COL_0 | hwEnum.TOP_UP
'disp1PanelsEnd
' (a third display is the same block with DISP2_, disp2Panels, disp2PanelsEnd and PIN_GROUP_P0_P15)

' ---- Optional settings: remove the leading ' from both lines of the one you want ----
'#DEFINE DISP0_ROTATED
'CON DISP0_ROTATION = hwEnum.TOP_TO_RIGHT
'#DEFINE DISP0_REFRESH_GIVEN
'CON DISP0_TARGET_REFRESH_HZ = 30

' ================================== END USER SECTION ==================================

CON ' ---- Defaults (not edited) ----

'  Each optional setting not switched on above takes its default here, and each display not
'  present gets an empty panel list: it has no panels and its buffers cost no memory.

    DEFAULT_REFRESH_HZ      = 60                                ' the refresh rate the driver aims for

#IFNDEF DISP0_ROTATED
CON
    DISP0_ROTATION          = hwEnum.AS_BUILT
#ENDIF
#IFNDEF DISP0_REFRESH_GIVEN
CON
    DISP0_TARGET_REFRESH_HZ = DEFAULT_REFRESH_HZ
#ENDIF

#IFNDEF DISP1_PRESENT
CON
    DISP1_ADAPTER_BASE_PIN  = hwEnum.PIN_GROUP_P32_P47
    DISP1_PANEL_DRIVER_CHIP = hwEnum.CHIP_UNKNOWN
    DISP1_PANEL_COLUMNS     = 0
    DISP1_PANEL_ROWS        = 0
    DISP1_COLOR_DEPTH       = hwEnum.DEPTH_8BIT
DAT
disp1Panels
disp1PanelsEnd
#ENDIF
#IFNDEF DISP1_ROTATED
CON
    DISP1_ROTATION          = hwEnum.AS_BUILT
#ENDIF
#IFNDEF DISP1_REFRESH_GIVEN
CON
    DISP1_TARGET_REFRESH_HZ = DEFAULT_REFRESH_HZ
#ENDIF

#IFNDEF DISP2_PRESENT
CON
    DISP2_ADAPTER_BASE_PIN  = hwEnum.PIN_GROUP_P0_P15
    DISP2_PANEL_DRIVER_CHIP = hwEnum.CHIP_UNKNOWN
    DISP2_PANEL_COLUMNS     = 0
    DISP2_PANEL_ROWS        = 0
    DISP2_COLOR_DEPTH       = hwEnum.DEPTH_8BIT
DAT
disp2Panels
disp2PanelsEnd
#ENDIF
#IFNDEF DISP2_ROTATED
CON
    DISP2_ROTATION          = hwEnum.AS_BUILT
#ENDIF
#IFNDEF DISP2_REFRESH_GIVEN
CON
    DISP2_TARGET_REFRESH_HZ = DEFAULT_REFRESH_HZ
#ENDIF

CON ' ---- Storage sizes (not edited) ----

'  Every buffer is sized from its display's panel count, the length of its panel list:
'  (dispNPanelsEnd - dispNPanels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG. A CON cannot count a DAT list, so
'  the sizes are written out in the DAT section below. Hub RAM is the only limit on the panel
'  count the compiler applies; a display too large for hub RAM does not compile.

    BYTES_PER_COLOR         = 3                                 ' the screen buffer holds one byte each of R, G, B
    PIXELS_PER_PWM_BYTE     = 2                                 ' a PWM frame holds 4 bits per pixel

    ' The layout tables of one display (isp_hub75_hwBufferAccess.spin2 builds and reads them),
    ' in one block: first the LONG tables of one entry per grid cell, then the BYTE tables of
    ' one entry per panel, then the BYTE tables of one entry per grid cell. The panels form one
    ' piece, so N panels fit a grid of ((N + 2) / 2) x ((N + 1) / 2) cells.
    LAYOUT_LONGS_PER_CELL   = 3                                 ' cell offset, right step, down step
    LAYOUT_BYTES_PER_PANEL  = 8                                 ' the per-panel position tables
    LAYOUT_BYTES_PER_CELL   = 2                                 ' the layout grid and the mounted grid
    GRID_LONG_SIDE_EXTRA    = 2                                 ' grid cells: ((N + 2) / 2) x ((N + 1) / 2)
    GRID_SHORT_SIDE_EXTRA   = 1
    GRID_SIDES              = 2

    ' guard patterns around the first display's buffers; nothing reads them
    GUARD_FRONT             = $0DF0ADDE
    GUARD_BACK              = $0DF1ADDE
    GUARD_TABLES            = $0DF2ADDE

DAT ' ---- Storage (not edited) ----

' DISP0: screen buffer, two PWM frame sets, layout tables
disp0Guard      LONG    GUARD_FRONT
disp0Screen     LONG    0[((((disp0PanelsEnd - disp0Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) * DISP0_PANEL_COLUMNS * DISP0_PANEL_ROWS * BYTES_PER_COLOR) + hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG - 1) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG]
disp0Frames1    LONG    0[DISP0_COLOR_DEPTH * ((((((disp0PanelsEnd - disp0Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) * DISP0_PANEL_COLUMNS * DISP0_PANEL_ROWS) / PIXELS_PER_PWM_BYTE) + hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG - 1) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG)]
disp0Frames2    LONG    0[DISP0_COLOR_DEPTH * ((((((disp0PanelsEnd - disp0Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) * DISP0_PANEL_COLUMNS * DISP0_PANEL_ROWS) / PIXELS_PER_PWM_BYTE) + hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG - 1) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG)]
disp0GuardBack  LONG    GUARD_BACK
disp0Tables     LONG    0[(LAYOUT_LONGS_PER_CELL * ((((disp0PanelsEnd - disp0Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) + GRID_LONG_SIDE_EXTRA) / GRID_SIDES) * ((((disp0PanelsEnd - disp0Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) + GRID_SHORT_SIDE_EXTRA) / GRID_SIDES)) + ((((LAYOUT_BYTES_PER_PANEL * ((disp0PanelsEnd - disp0Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG)) + (LAYOUT_BYTES_PER_CELL * ((((disp0PanelsEnd - disp0Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) + GRID_LONG_SIDE_EXTRA) / GRID_SIDES) * ((((disp0PanelsEnd - disp0Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) + GRID_SHORT_SIDE_EXTRA) / GRID_SIDES))) + hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG - 1) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG)]
disp0GuardTbl   LONG    GUARD_TABLES

' DISP1: screen buffer, two PWM frame sets, layout tables (zero length when not present)
disp1Screen     LONG    0[((((disp1PanelsEnd - disp1Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) * DISP1_PANEL_COLUMNS * DISP1_PANEL_ROWS * BYTES_PER_COLOR) + hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG - 1) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG]
disp1Frames1    LONG    0[DISP1_COLOR_DEPTH * ((((((disp1PanelsEnd - disp1Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) * DISP1_PANEL_COLUMNS * DISP1_PANEL_ROWS) / PIXELS_PER_PWM_BYTE) + hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG - 1) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG)]
disp1Frames2    LONG    0[DISP1_COLOR_DEPTH * ((((((disp1PanelsEnd - disp1Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) * DISP1_PANEL_COLUMNS * DISP1_PANEL_ROWS) / PIXELS_PER_PWM_BYTE) + hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG - 1) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG)]
disp1Tables     LONG    0[(LAYOUT_LONGS_PER_CELL * ((((disp1PanelsEnd - disp1Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) + GRID_LONG_SIDE_EXTRA) / GRID_SIDES) * ((((disp1PanelsEnd - disp1Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) + GRID_SHORT_SIDE_EXTRA) / GRID_SIDES)) + ((((LAYOUT_BYTES_PER_PANEL * ((disp1PanelsEnd - disp1Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG)) + (LAYOUT_BYTES_PER_CELL * ((((disp1PanelsEnd - disp1Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) + GRID_LONG_SIDE_EXTRA) / GRID_SIDES) * ((((disp1PanelsEnd - disp1Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) + GRID_SHORT_SIDE_EXTRA) / GRID_SIDES))) + hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG - 1) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG)]

' DISP2: screen buffer, two PWM frame sets, layout tables (zero length when not present)
disp2Screen     LONG    0[((((disp2PanelsEnd - disp2Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) * DISP2_PANEL_COLUMNS * DISP2_PANEL_ROWS * BYTES_PER_COLOR) + hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG - 1) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG]
disp2Frames1    LONG    0[DISP2_COLOR_DEPTH * ((((((disp2PanelsEnd - disp2Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) * DISP2_PANEL_COLUMNS * DISP2_PANEL_ROWS) / PIXELS_PER_PWM_BYTE) + hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG - 1) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG)]
disp2Frames2    LONG    0[DISP2_COLOR_DEPTH * ((((((disp2PanelsEnd - disp2Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) * DISP2_PANEL_COLUMNS * DISP2_PANEL_ROWS) / PIXELS_PER_PWM_BYTE) + hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG - 1) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG)]
disp2Tables     LONG    0[(LAYOUT_LONGS_PER_CELL * ((((disp2PanelsEnd - disp2Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) + GRID_LONG_SIDE_EXTRA) / GRID_SIDES) * ((((disp2PanelsEnd - disp2Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) + GRID_SHORT_SIDE_EXTRA) / GRID_SIDES)) + ((((LAYOUT_BYTES_PER_PANEL * ((disp2PanelsEnd - disp2Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG)) + (LAYOUT_BYTES_PER_CELL * ((((disp2PanelsEnd - disp2Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) + GRID_LONG_SIDE_EXTRA) / GRID_SIDES) * ((((disp2PanelsEnd - disp2Panels) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG) + GRID_SHORT_SIDE_EXTRA) / GRID_SIDES))) + hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG - 1) / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG)]

OBJ

    hwEnum      : "isp_hub75_hwEnums"                               ' hub75 attachment, set up constants

PUB null()
'' Placeholder to prevent this object from being used as a top-level file.
''

PUB panelList(eHub75Adapter) : pPanels, nListBytes
'' Return one display's panel list: the address of its first sentence and the list's length in
'' bytes (one LONG per panel, so the panel count is nListBytes / hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG). The
'' adapter set-up (isp_hub75_hwBufferAccess.spin2) reads it; programs do not.
''
'' @param eHub75Adapter - the HUB75 adapter (hwEnum.HUB75_ADAPTER_1 .. HUB75_ADAPTER_3; adapter k drives DISP(k-1))
'' @returns pPanels - hub address of the display's first panel sentence (0 for any other value)
'' @returns nListBytes - the list's length in bytes (0 for a display that is not present)

    pPanels := nListBytes := 0
    case eHub75Adapter
        hwEnum.HUB75_ADAPTER_1:
            pPanels := @disp0Panels
            nListBytes := @disp0PanelsEnd - @disp0Panels
        hwEnum.HUB75_ADAPTER_2:
            pPanels := @disp1Panels
            nListBytes := @disp1PanelsEnd - @disp1Panels
        hwEnum.HUB75_ADAPTER_3:
            pPanels := @disp2Panels
            nListBytes := @disp2PanelsEnd - @disp2Panels

PUB displayStorage(eHub75Adapter) : pScreen, pFrameSet1, pFrameSet2, pTables
'' Return the addresses of one display's storage: its screen buffer (BYTES_PER_COLOR bytes per
'' pixel), its two PWM frame sets (depth x pixels / PIXELS_PER_PWM_BYTE bytes each) and its
'' layout-table block (the LAYOUT_ sizes above), each sized here from the display's panel count.
'' The adapter set-up (isp_hub75_hwBufferAccess.spin2) reads it; programs do not.
''
'' @param eHub75Adapter - the HUB75 adapter (hwEnum.HUB75_ADAPTER_1 .. HUB75_ADAPTER_3; adapter k drives DISP(k-1))
'' @returns pScreen - hub address of the screen buffer (0 for any other value)
'' @returns pFrameSet1 - hub address of PWM frame set 1
'' @returns pFrameSet2 - hub address of PWM frame set 2
'' @returns pTables - hub address of the layout-table block

    pScreen := pFrameSet1 := pFrameSet2 := pTables := 0
    case eHub75Adapter
        hwEnum.HUB75_ADAPTER_1:
            pScreen, pFrameSet1, pFrameSet2, pTables := @disp0Screen, @disp0Frames1, @disp0Frames2, @disp0Tables
        hwEnum.HUB75_ADAPTER_2:
            pScreen, pFrameSet1, pFrameSet2, pTables := @disp1Screen, @disp1Frames1, @disp1Frames2, @disp1Tables
        hwEnum.HUB75_ADAPTER_3:
            pScreen, pFrameSet1, pFrameSet2, pTables := @disp2Screen, @disp2Frames1, @disp2Frames2, @disp2Tables

